Extend the AD9361/AD9363 RF LO range to 46.875 MHz - 6 GHz

ADI specifies the AD9363 only from 325 MHz to 3.8 GHz and limits it to that
range in the driver (and the AD9361 RX to 70 MHz and up). This patch lifts
both limits to the full VCO/divider range, as on the usual Pluto
modification. The PLLs lock over the whole range, but sensitivity, image
rejection, LO leakage and the front-end match outside 325 MHz - 3.8 GHz are
not specified by ADI and vary between boards.

The RF PLL clock runs at half the LO frequency, so the lowest frequency
accepted is 46875002 Hz, not MIN_*_CARRIER_FREQ_HZ itself.

--- /dev/null
+++ linux-04fbdbb433faae8ffb3a5b24b7435509b11334cb/drivers/iio/adc/ad9361_regs.h
@@ -2817,11 +2817,11 @@
 #define MIN_VCO_FREQ_HZ			6000000000ULL
 
 #define MAX_CARRIER_FREQ_HZ		6000000000ULL
-#define MIN_RX_CARRIER_FREQ_HZ		70000000ULL
+#define MIN_RX_CARRIER_FREQ_HZ		46875001ULL
 #define MIN_TX_CARRIER_FREQ_HZ		46875001ULL
 
-#define AD9363A_MAX_CARRIER_FREQ_HZ	3800000000ULL
-#define AD9363A_MIN_CARRIER_FREQ_HZ	325000000ULL
+#define AD9363A_MAX_CARRIER_FREQ_HZ	6000000000ULL
+#define AD9363A_MIN_CARRIER_FREQ_HZ	46875001ULL
 
 #define MAX_GAIN_TABLE_SIZE		90
 #define MAX_NUM_GAIN_TABLES		16 /* randomly picked */
